DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260521T203000
UID:260518YUs74_nZpkuNbiVD7iBf0A
DESCRIPTION:An evening of conversation with Paldrom Catharine Collins\, ba
 sed on her memoir Girl in a Box: Seeking Enlightenment as a Tibetan Buddh
 ist Nun. As a wide-eyed spiritual seeker from Oklahoma\, she sought enligh
 tenment\, centered on the desire for transformation\, and the promises of 
 the path. Paldrom will draw us into her search\, the pull of spiritual tea
 chers and teachings\, and what began to emerge when the path no longer unf
 olded as expected.
LOCATION:Many Rivers Books & Tea
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/girl-in-a-box/18922098/
 2026-05-21T19
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SIR Branch 17 – Emergence of Artificial Intelligence in Medicine
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260521T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260521T133000
UID:260514hGMjIzQyZUaMuW-t7871VQ
DESCRIPTION:Enrich Your Life – SIR Branch 17 – **Emergence of Artifici
 al Intelligence in Medicine.**\n\n**SIR Branch 17** will hold its next mee
 ting on Thursday\, May 21\, 2026.  Our speaker will be Dr. Brian Schmidt 
 who will talk about the Emergence of Artificial Intelligence in Medicine T
 oday and its Applications in the Future.  Dr. Schmidt helped start the la
 paroscopic program as well as the trauma service at Santa Rosa Memorial Ho
 spital.  He runs the trauma service as the medical director at Memorial H
 ospital.\n\n**RESERVATIONS REQUIRED**.  Members pay for lunch but its Fre
 e for invited first-time guests.  Contact us for more details on how to r
 eceive an invitation.\n\nSIR\, Inc. is a California non-profit organizatio
 n that provides social activities for men and their partners whose mission
  is: “To enhance the lives of our members through fun activities\, lunch
 eons and events while making Friends for Life”.\n\nSIR Branch 17 meets i
 n Santa Rosa for socializing\, lunch\, and an interesting speaker every 3r
 d Thursday of the month.  In addition to our luncheon\, we organize other
  activities\, including Golf\, Bocce\, Poker\, Bridge\, Dining Out (with &
  without partners)\; Global Affairs\; Pickleball\; Coffee Club\; Beer\, Wi
 ne & Spirits\; Book Club\; Hiking/Walking\; and more!\n\nLive longer and h
 appier with good friends while enjoying fun activities.  We don’t raise
  money\, have a political agenda\, a religious orientation\, or sell anyth
 ing.  For more information\, visit us at www.SIR17.org or contact us by p
