BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:H&L Live: Marshall House Project
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T153000
UID:260519ezgiJsLQ4ECA5BbIYkZpmQ
DESCRIPTION:Welcome to H&L Live—our new concert series on the vineyard s
 tage! Join us Saturday\, May 23rd for an afternoon of live music\, wood-fi
 red pizza\, and wine country vibes as Marshall House Project lights up our
  outdoor venue.\n\nMarshall House Project is the North Bay's 2025 Best Fu
 nk Band\, and once you hear them\, you'll know why. Born on Marshall Drive
  in Santa Rosa\, this powerhouse ensemble blends blues\, rock\, funk\, reg
 gae\, and soul into an original sound designed to keep you dancing. With u
 plifting music full of twists and turns\, conscious lyrics\, and sizzling 
 guitar solos\, Marshall House Project creates the kind of energy that make
 s Friday afternoons unforgettable.\n\nThis is what our new stage was built
  for: great artists\, beautiful afternoons\, and the Russian River Valley 
 as your backdrop. Bring a blanket\, grab a glass\, and settle in for one o
 f those perfect wine country moments.\n\nWhat to Know:\n\nAdmission is fre
 e - just show up and enjoy\n\nPizza & Chill Red: Fresh wood-fired pizza p
 aired with our new Chill Red\n\nOutdoor seating - Lawn and picnic area av
 ailable \\(bring blankets encouraged\\)\n\nAll ages welcome - Family-frie
 ndly event\n\nWine available for purchase by the glass or bottle\n\nThis 
 is the first of our H&L Live series—a celebration of our outdoor stage\,
  our community\, and the artists who make wine country special. Come for t
 he music\, stay for the pizza\, and remember why Saturdays in Sonoma Count
 y are the best.\n\nLearn more about Marshall House Project: marshallhouse
 project.com
LOCATION:Hook & Ladder Winery
URL:https://www.hookandladderwinery.com/event/hl-live-marshall-house-proje
 ct
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Social Contractors: Live & Free @ Lagunitas Tap Room
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T180000
UID:260519NGAaUNBnGE-b3-1GOd7--w
DESCRIPTION:“….Get ready for the super-entertaining sounds of local ba
 nd The Social Contractors. They totally rock\, in all the right ways…”
  - Argus-Courier\n\nJoin The Social Contractors from 3:30-6 PM on Saturday
 \, 5/23 as they return to Lagunitas Tap room for an afternoon and evening 
 of upbeat original progressive alternative rock and their own spin on clas
 sic hits from the 60s-90s (The Beatles\, The Doors\, Jimi Hendrix\, Pink F
 loyd\, Steely Dan\, The Police\, Men At Work\, U2\, Tears for Fears\, Tom 
 Petty\, Gerry Rafferty\, and more). \n\nWhether you like melodic vocals\,
  searing guitar and sax solos\, intriguing lyrics\, or just great dynamic 
 and danceable rhythms\, The Social Contractors won't disappoint.\n\nThe So
 cial Contractors lineup for this free live performance features band found
 er and songwriter\, Jason E Davies (lead vocals\, lead/rhythm guitar)\, Tr
 avis Thayer (sax/keys/vocals)\, Rob Neidel (bass/vocals)\, Chris Oatman (d
 rums).\n\nThe Lagunitas Tap Room is one of Petaluma's finest brew pubs and
  outdoor music venues\, featuring an exquisite selection of fine craft bee
 rs on tap in addition to excellent alcohol-free beverages. Couple this wit
 h an array of enticing appetizers\, gourmet burgers\, and salads\, positiv
 e socialization\, and general cheer in a festive setting with free live mu
 sic means a "splendid time is guaranteed for all"
LOCATION:Lagunitas Brewing Company
URL:https://lagunitas.com/taproom/petaluma/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
