BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Room in the Castle - Live Theatre
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T190000
UID:260505jx_L1eX2AkWeuOSGQwvIsQ
DESCRIPTION:A Room in the Castle is a feminist reimagining of William Shak
 espeare’s Hamlet\, written by prolific American playwright Lauren M. Gu
 nderson. The play shifts the perspective of the classic tragedy to focus e
 ntirely on the women of Elsinore: Ophelia\, Queen Gertrude\, and Ophelia
 ’s handmaid\, Anna.\n\nThe troubled\, grieving Prince of Denmark is neve
 r far from the thoughts of Ophelia\, a caretaker to Ophelia\, and the Quee
 n of Denmark. Playwright Lauren Gunderson does a masterful job re-imaginin
 g the women trapped by class\, circumstances\, expectations\, and desire w
 ithin the castle’s walls. Each\, in their own way\, follows the queen’
 s edict for women—to “obey\, agree\, assist”—until they absolutely
  do not. This play dances and duels with Hamlet\, foregrounding the women 
 in the play and re-imagining them with agency\, vitality\, and radical hea
 rts eager for a more hopeful ending.\n\nThe women of Hamlet have moments t
 hat are wholly their own. They own the stage—and our hearts.  ­— DC 
 TheaterArts\n\nFeaturing: Tatiana – Luisa Sermol / Ophelia – Marie Sad
 d / Gertrude – Leontyne Mbele Mbong\n\nDirected by Amy Kossow: "I have s
 een Hamlet so many times but here finally is a chance to stop and ask what
  the women are doing while all the men plot and scheme.  Lauren Gunderson
  gives Gertrude and Ophelia \\(along with a mysterious third woman\\) a wh
 ole play all to themselves\, and as the events of Hamlet unfold around the
 m\, these three create their own brilliant stories.\n\n- Sponsored in part
  by Melinda & Paul Pressler -\n\n-Theatre - Programmed by Aldo Billingslea
  and Amy Kossow -
LOCATION:THE 222 / Healdsburg
URL:https://the222.org/product/a-room-in-the-castle/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:INTO THE LIGHT: Light-filled aintings by Katy Boggs
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T170000
UID:260501vz4-Nwz9eUOsQGUKQLSi1w
DESCRIPTION:Katy's paintings are an exploration of light—how it shapes f
 orm\, reveals color\, and defines what we see.\n\n"I am drawn to moments w
 here light is felt as much as seen: filtering through dense leaves\, tower
 ing in the crowns of trees\, glinting off cresting waves\, or softening in
 to the quiet glow of a sunset. Light is everywhere\; without it\, there is
  no seeing. Beyond its physical presence\, it also carries a deeper resona
 nce as a symbol of hope. In a time of uncertainty\, this work seeks to bri
 ng light into the image\, both visually and metaphorically."\n\nReception:
  April 25\, 4 to 6 pm.
LOCATION:Sebastopol Gallery
URL:http://sebastopolgallery.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
