BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BFA Exhibition
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T160000
UID:2604179oj5a-BoOkCJS5MTV1p6mg
DESCRIPTION:Each spring\, the University Art Gallery proudly presents the 
 Bachelor of Fine Arts \\(BFA\\) Exhibition\, showcasing the work of Sonoma
  State University's graduating BFA class. The 2026 BFA Exhibition will be 
 on view April 23-May 23\, 2026. Offered by SSU's Art Department\, the BFA 
 degree is distinguished from the BA by its rigorous\, studio-intensive cur
 riculum. The program requires an additional year of focused study\, includ
 ing advanced coursework in studio art\, art history\, and art theory. Ofte
 n regarded as the degree of choice for students pursuing graduate or profe
 ssional studies\, the BFA fosters significant artistic development within 
 a concentrated creative environment. For both students and faculty\, this 
 exhibition represents a culminating achievement-an opportunity to present 
 a carefully curated selection of each artist's strongest work in a profess
 ional gallery setting\, exhibited alongside their peers. Opening Reception
 : Thursday\, April 23\, 2026 4:00-6:00 pm
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/bfa-exhibition/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ronstadt Revolution at The California Theatre
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T220000
UID:260413t3QowsjPWkCeEQoYHPHHAQ
DESCRIPTION:Experience a heartfelt tribute to Linda Ronstadt at The Califo
 rnia Theatre with Ronstadt Revolution\, Northern California's premier homa
 ge to the 11-time Grammy winner. Led by acclaimed vocalist Natalie Amaya\,
  the band features seasoned musicians who have performed alongside legends
  like Elvis Presley\, Tina Turner\, and Sheryl Crow. Together\, they bring
  Ronstadt's iconic catalog to life with authenticity and soul\, celebratin
 g both her English and Spanish-language hits. Audiences can enjoy favorite
 s like "Heat Wave\," "You're No Good\," "Blue Bayou\," and "Tu Solo Tu\," 
 performed with passion and precision. This dynamic live show offers a joyf
 ul journey through the timeless music that defined a generation.
LOCATION:The California
URL:https://www.sonoma.com/event/ronstadt-revolution-at-the-california-the
 atre/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Stargazing at Mount Burdell
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T201500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T221500
UID:260401g6y5lA_NM0OltckPoMBuyQ
DESCRIPTION:Directions:\n\nTo be provided only upon successful RSVP\n\nSpo
 nsor: Parks\n\nAccommodation Information: If you are a person with a disab
 ility and require an accommodation to participate in a County program\, se
 rvice\, or activity\, requests may be made by calling 415-473- 4381 \\(Voi
 ce\\)\, Dial 711 for CA Relay\, or by submitting a\n\nDisability Accommoda
 tion Request\n\nat least five business days in advance of the event. We wi
 ll do our best to fulfill requests received with less than five business d
 ays' notice. Copies of documents are available in alternative formats upon
  request.\n\nJoin Ranger Gabe and the Marin Stargazers on Mount Burdell fo
 r an evening of stargazing. Weather permitting\, we'll observe the Moon\, 
 where you'll see visible craters and mountains. Additionally\, the planets
  Venus and Jupiter will be visible. Jupiter's moon\, Io\, will also featur
 e a rar e "shadow transit." Friendly dogs are welcome but must be le ashed
 . Dress in layers\, wear sturdy shoes\, bring a red headlamp or fla shligh
 t\, and binoculars if you have them. Be prepared for a 0.5-mile walk on un
 even ground to and from the viewing area. Adverse weather or poor air qual
 ity may result in cancellation. Check the calendar or call \\(415\\) 473-2
 816 two hours before the event to confirm the status. Registration is requ
 ired.\n\nQuestions: Contact\n\nGabe Ngarangad
LOCATION:Mount
URL:http://www.trumba.com/https%20://www.marincounty.gov/disability-accomm
 odation-request
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
