SUMMARY:The Social Contractors Rock Murphy's Irish Pub!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T203000
UID:260519sN93wAf8r0uCj6pjOO9QPg
DESCRIPTION:“….Get ready for the super-entertaining sounds of local ba
 nd The Social Contractors. They totally rock\, in all the right ways…”
  - Argus-Courier\n\nJoin The Social Contractors from 5:30-8:30 PM on Sunda
 y\, 5/24 as they return to rock Murphy's Irish Pub with an evening of upbe
 at original progressive alternative rock and their own spin on classic hit
 s from the 60s-90s (The Beatles\, The Doors\, Jimi Hendrix\, Pink Floyd\, 
 Steely Dan\, The Police\, Men At Work\, U2\, Tears for Fears\, Tom Petty\,
  Gerry Rafferty\, and more).\n\nWhether you like melodic vocals\, searing 
 guitar and sax solos\, intriguing lyrics\, captivating songs\, or just gre
 at dynamic and danceable rhythms\, The Social Contractors won't disappoint
 .\n\nThe Social Contractors lineup for this free live performance features
  band founder and songwriter\, Jason E Davies (lead vocals\, lead/rhythm g
 uitar)\, Travis Thayer (sax/keys/vocals)\, Alex Fabian-Davies (bass)\, and
  Chris Oatman (drums).\n\nLocated in the heart of historic downtown Sonoma
 \, Murphy's Irish Pub is the place to be for a lively atmosphere of music\
 , social merriment\, and a diverse menu of delicious food\, and satisfying
  full bar beverage options.
LOCATION:Murphy's Irish Pub & Restaurant
URL:https://www.sonomapub.com/events
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Stella Heath & Ian Scherer
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T143000
UID:260519jeAePIoVOU64iCt01vkRLQ
DESCRIPTION:Intimate Interplay: Stella Heath & Ian Scherer\n\nJoin us for 
 No Cell Sundays with Stella Heath and Ian Scherer\, a duo whose decade-lon
 g musical partnership creates something truly extraordinary.\n\nHarkening 
 to the classic duo recordings of Ella Fitzgerald and Joe Pass\, their soun
 d is grounded in the art of interplay—where melody\, harmony\, and impro
 visation unfold in real time. With just voice and guitar\, they create a r
 ichly textured and intimate musical experience\, marked by sensitivity\, s
 pontaneity\, and a shared musical language that can only come from years o
 f collaboration.\n\nTheir repertoire draws from the Great American Songboo
 k while also embracing more modern selections\, each reimagined through th
 eir distinct approach. Whether in a quiet listening room or on a concert s
 tage\, Stella Heath and Ian Scherer invite audiences into a space of conne
 ction—where every phrase is shaped in the moment\, and each performance 
 is uniquely alive.\n\nWhat's No Cell Sundays? It's simple: disconnect from
  your devices\, reconnect with great wine\, live music\, and the people ar
 ound you. Check your phone with us at the door and receive a complimentar
 y tasting. Bring a blanket\, grab a glass\, and spend your Sunday the way
  it was meant to be spent.
LOCATION:Hook & Ladder Winery
URL:https://www.hookandladderwinery.com/event/no-cell-sundays-stella-ian
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
