BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Soda Club Firing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T170000
UID:2605084IDgPGn_jk2DaMNHbyAMyQ
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nSaturday\, May 23 from 10:00 AM – 5:00 PM Sunday
 \, May 24 from 10:00 Am – 6:00 PM Tuesday\, May 26 from 4:00 PM – 7:00
  PM\n\nLocation\n\nKiln Shed\n\nExperience Level\n\nIntermediate and Advan
 ced\n\nEvent Categories: Ceramics\, Workshops\n\nAge\\(s\\)\n\n18 and olde
 r\n\nRegistration\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$100\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\nInclu
 ded\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$100\n\nJoin the Julia Soda Firing Club
  for regular cone 6 soda firings—no formal instruction\, just shared kil
 n access and 1 cubic foot of firing space.\n\nAbout the Class\n\nPrerequis
 ites to enroll in Soda Firing Club\n\nMust have taken at least one\, Intro
  to Mid-Range Soda Firing Workshop\n\nBe well versed in protocols for load
 ing the soda kiln\, kiln safety\, equipment and operating safety\, and be 
 willing and able to be unsupervised with the kiln during loading\, unloadi
 ng\, and post firing cleaning of the kiln.\n\nMust have pre-approval from 
 the Director of Ceramics\n\nThe “Julia” Soda Firing Club is designed f
 or folks looking for longterm use with our Soda Kiln\, Julia. The club is 
 led by Studio Monitors\, and a Studio Technician but involves no formal in
 struction in soda firing processes. Without a formalized instructor\, our 
 Soda Club offers a more financially accessible way of having work soda-fir
 ed\, without the need to retake our Intro to Soda Firing workshop courses.
  The Soda Club will run firings monthly or as often as desired and needed 
 depending on participant interest. Unlike our Soda Firing Workshops\, club
  firings will include no instruction on wadding\, slips\, glazes\, or any 
 lectures on the subject of soda firing. As such\, participants must feel c
 omfortable with the safety and care of the equipment\, as well as loading\
 , firing\, and maintenance procedures surrounding the firing process. Each
  participant gets 1 cubic foot of firing space. Tip: Make sure all your po
 ts fit approximately into a milk crate which is 1 cubic foot of space. Thi
 s firing will be chosen by the group to be either oxidation or reduction\,
  and fired to cone 6 with sprayed soda at the end.\n\nMembership has its b
 enefits\n\nAll Silver Memberships and above receive 10% off the registrati
 on cost for any class purchase over $40. Materials fees are not discounted
 .\n\nBecome a member today and find community\, connection\, and creativit
 y.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/soda-club-firing/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Solage Memorial Day Weekend
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T000000
UID:260506V4U9Eedbn0-iwt1itw0LXA
DESCRIPTION:WELCOME TO SOLAGE \n\nA fresh and vibrant Napa Valley retreat\
 n\nA century ago\, Calistoga was a haven of natural hot springs and sun-so
 aked landscapes\, embodying the easy charm of Napa Valley. Today\, it’s 
 a coveted destination for wine lovers\, food enthusiasts\, and wellness se
 ekers chasing the “good life.” Solage captures this spirit\, welcoming
  visitors and local vintners alike to unwind after a day in the vineyards
 –sipping wine or craft cocktails\, savoring the moment\, and embracing t
 his little slice of paradise we like to call home.
LOCATION:Solage\, Auberge Resorts Collection
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108311567?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Room in the Castle - Live Theatre
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T140000
UID:260505vmA_VBVAGEyAJXc7jeZUig
DESCRIPTION:A Room in the Castle is a feminist reimagining of William Shak
 espeare’s Hamlet\, written by prolific American playwright Lauren M. Gu
 nderson. The play shifts the perspective of the classic tragedy to focus e
 ntirely on the women of Elsinore: Ophelia\, Queen Gertrude\, and Ophelia
 ’s handmaid\, Anna.\n\nThe troubled\, grieving Prince of Denmark is neve
 r far from the thoughts of Ophelia\, a caretaker to Ophelia\, and the Quee
 n of Denmark. Playwright Lauren Gunderson does a masterful job re-imaginin
 g the women trapped by class\, circumstances\, expectations\, and desire w
 ithin the castle’s walls. Each\, in their own way\, follows the queen’
 s edict for women—to “obey\, agree\, assist”—until they absolutely
  do not. This play dances and duels with Hamlet\, foregrounding the women 
 in the play and re-imagining them with agency\, vitality\, and radical hea
 rts eager for a more hopeful ending.\n\nThe women of Hamlet have moments t
 hat are wholly their own. They own the stage—and our hearts.  ­— DC 
 TheaterArts\n\nFeaturing: Tatiana – Luisa Sermol / Ophelia – Marie Sad
 d / Gertrude – Leontyne Mbele Mbong\n\nDirected by Amy Kossow: "I have s
 een Hamlet so many times but here finally is a chance to stop and ask what
  the women are doing while all the men plot and scheme.  Lauren Gunderson
  gives Gertrude and Ophelia \\(along with a mysterious third woman\\) a wh
 ole play all to themselves\, and as the events of Hamlet unfold around the
 m\, these three create their own brilliant stories.\n\n- Sponsored in part
  by Melinda & Paul Pressler -\n\n-Theatre - Programmed by Aldo Billingslea
  and Amy Kossow -
LOCATION:THE 222 / Healdsburg
URL:https://the222.org/product/a-room-in-the-castle/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
