 . Our subjects will be flora and fauna - a sampling of plants and animals 
 - fruits\, florals\, foliage\, and four legged friends. These subjects are
  great for beginners and experienced watercolor painters alike\; their org
 anic shapes make them forgiving drawing subjects\, but their beauty can be
  a muse for life. Over the course of the class we will progress through 3 
 compositions\, graduating from simpler to more complex forms. This class w
 ill work from life and from photos\, practicing basic drawing skills in ad
 dition to watercolor technique. With six class sessions\, participants wil
 l have the opportunity to develop their skills and build muscle memory wit
 h a medium that often feels like it has a mind of its own. All skill level
