BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The California Honeydrops | Cookout Concert Series
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260525T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260525T180000
UID:260325hh7SWB8btkmsDMHn6AqBYw
DESCRIPTION:KC TURNER PRESENTS  THE CALIFORNIA HONEYDROPS BottleRock After
 Dark 13th Annual COOKOUT CONCERT SERIES HOPMONK NOVATO OUTDOOR VENUE Spons
 ored by JAMBAR MOSTLY STANDING ON GROUND LEVEL LIMITED SEATING ON LAWN & T
 OP OF HILL ALL AGES ABOUT: “The California Honeydrops...evoke the greasy
  rumble of Booker T and channel the spiritual ecstasy of Sly and the Famil
 y Stone.” -Rolling Stone Formed in the subway systems of Oakland\, retro
 -soul outfit The California Honeydrops are an electrifying group that defy
  convention at every turn. They’ve become a mainstay at festivals includ
 ing Byron Bay Bluesfest \\(Australia\\)\, Outside Lands\, Monterey Jazz\, 
 Lightning In A Bottle\, and touring with B.B. King\, Dr. John\, Bonnie Rai
 tt\, Buddy Guy\, and Allen Toussaint. Led by the enigmatic and energetic f
 rontman\, Lech Wierzynski\, and percussionist Benjamin Malament\, each mem
 ber of the band is a virtuoso in their own rite — Yanos “Johnny Bones
 ” Lustig on saxophone\, Lorenzo Loera on keyboards/guitar\, Beaumont Bea
 ullieu on drums\, Miles Blackwell on bass\, and regularly accompanied by O
 liver Tuttle on trombone\, Leon Cotter on saxophone/clarinet\, and Miles L
 yons on trombone/sousaphone — navigating through a vast repertoire of or
 iginal songs and timeless classics every night. But what truly sets them a
 part is their unwavering commitment to the art of improvisation - a skill 
 so finely honed that they have completely abandoned the use of set lists a
 nd no two shows are ever the same. Off stage\, their music has been stream
 ed more than 200 million times\, and placed in a variety of TV and films\,
  including “Dead To Me\,” “Alaska Daily\,” “Black-ish” and mor
 e. Their new album “Redwood Highway” was released August 8\, 2025. ---
 -------------------------------- EVENT INFO: Q: Is this show outdoors? A: 
 Yes. This event is held in HopMonk Novato's outdoor concert venue. Q: Are 
 kids allowed? A: The shows are all ages. Kids need a ticket to attend. No 
 babies in arms. Q: Is there seating? A: Seating is limited and is first co
 me. You're allowed a LOW-BACK chair in the lawn section. At the top of the
  hillside section there is table seating that is first come. We recommend 
 arriving at the time doors open. Some shows are open dance floor/standing 
 room only while others are mostly seated. Varies from show to show. Q: Is 
 there parking? A: Parking is free and there is plenty of it. NO PETS NO CO
 OLERS NO BACKPACKS NO OUTSIDE FOOD NO UMBRELLAS NO REFUNDS | ALL SALES FIN
 AL Tickets: After completing your purchase on See Tickets\, you will recei
 ve an email confirmation with your attached PDF ticket\\(s\\). You MUST pr
 int and bring your PDF tickets AND VALID PHOTO IDENTIFICATION to be admitt
 ed for the event. You may download the See Tickets app and show your ticke
 t on your mobile device for entry in lieu of printing.
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern Novato
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1724454618531426/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The 68th Annual Sonoma Valley Joint Memorial Day  Observance
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260525T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260525T140000
UID:260519LpvlZLdpSkmFJ1_hE22U_A
DESCRIPTION:The Sonoma Valley community will gather at 11:00 a.m. on Monda
 y\, May 25\, at Sonoma Veterans Memorial Park for the 68th Annual Sonoma V
 alley Joint Memorial Day Observance\, presented by the Sonoma Veterans Mem
 orial Park Association.\n\nThis year’s Guest of Honor and keynote speake
 r will be retired United States Marine Corps Colonel Harry “Bucky” Pet
 erson\, a Sonoma resident and distinguished 33-year Marine Corps veteran w
 hose service included combat and leadership assignments in Vietnam\, the M
 iddle East\, Somalia\, Kuwait\, Iraq\, and Afghanistan. During his militar
 y career\, Colonel Peterson commanded units ranging from rifle platoons in
  Vietnam to an entire Marine Infantry Regiment. Following his retirement i
 n 1999\, he returned to active duty after the September 11 attacks to help
  oversee Marine operations in Afghanistan and Iraq. His military honors in
 clude the Distinguished Service Medal\, the Defense Superior Service Medal
 \, two Legion of Merit awards\, and three Combat Action Ribbons.\n\nThe ce
 remony will include the traditional Grand March of Veterans\, with all vet
 erans encouraged to arrive by 10:30 a.m.\, as seating is limited. Addition
 al program highlights will include patriotic performances by the Sonoma Ho
 metown Band under the direction of Therese Pasquale Hill\; Color Guard pre
 sentations by both the United States Marine Corps and the Civil Air Patrol
  Cadet Color Guard\; and a Rifle Salute presented by local veterans’ org
 anizations.\n\nMusical tributes will feature the National Anthem performed
  by Miss Sonoma County 2026 Addison Carver\, “God Bless America” sung 
 by vocalist Cathy Slack\, and ceremonial selections by bagpiper John Noona
 n and bugler Therese Pasquale Hill. Korean War veteran Olyn Hicks will pre
 sent a Memorial Day poem\, while regional pageant titleholders will lead t
 he Pledge of Allegiance.\n\nAdditional participants will include Sonoma Ma
 yor Ron Wellander\, who will deliver an official proclamation\; Vietnam ve
 teran Gene Campagna\, who will offer the invocation\; and Reverend Peadar 
 A. Dalton\, who will deliver the benediction. The ceremony will also featu
 re a civilian aerial flyover provided by the Sonoma Sky Park Aviators.\n\n
 Serving as Master of Ceremonies will be Carl “Chip” H. Allen\, a gradu
 ate of the United States Naval Academy and former U.S. Navy Polaris submar
 ine officer.\n\nImmediately following the ceremony\, guests are invited to
  attend the complimentary “All-American Picnic” hosted by the three So
 noma Rotary Clubs and the Native Daughters of the Golden West at the Sonom
 a Veterans Memorial Building.\n\n Guests will also have an opportunity to
  contribute to the ongoing Star of Honor pledge drive\, which supports the
  preservation of Sonoma Veterans Memorial Park and its black marble Star o
 f Honor Fountain — a lasting tribute inspired by the late World War II N
 avy veteran James “Jim” L. Parks.
LOCATION:Sonoma Veterans Memorial Park
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/the-68th-annual-sonoma-
 valley-joint-memorial-day-observance/18903461/2026-05-25T11
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Memorial Day Weekend Adventure on the Russian River Railbikes
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260525T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260525T150000
UID:260516NTScWa-PeUuIDbLdD_kBbQ
DESCRIPTION:Looking for the perfect Memorial Day Weekend outing?\n\nCelebr
 ate the start of summer with Russian River Railbikes — Sonoma County
 ’s unforgettable outdoor railbike experience through vineyards\, redwood
 s and the the scenic Russian River.\n\nPedal easy-to-ride railbikes along 
 historic rail lines while enjoying:\n\nStunning river and redwood views\n\
 nFresh air and open spaces\n\nA fun experience for couples\, families\, an
 d groups\n\nOne-of-a-kind photo opportunities\n\nA perfect pairing with lo
 cal wineries\, breweries\, and coastal day trips\n\nMemorial Day weekend d
 epartures are filling quickly.\n\nReserve your Memorial Day Weekend ride n
 ow: www.russianriverrailbikes.org\n\nCreate a new Memorial Day tradition i
 n Sonoma County.
