BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tuesdays in the Plaza: The Sun Kings (Beatles Tribute)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260526T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260526T200000
UID:260514PARGMNIoxEObUYoAKBJuJQ
DESCRIPTION:Our weekly summer concerts in the Healdsburg Plaza from 6:00 p
 .m. to 8:00 p.m. provide an eclectic and unique line-up of bands\, and hav
 e been assembled to please a wide array of musical interests. Food vendors
  will be on-hand to offer locally sourced food for sale starting at 5:00 p
 .m. with the music beginning at 6:00 p.m.\n\nAbout the band: Enjoy the mu
 sic created by one of the most influential bands of our time. You'll hear 
 many of the Fab Four's \\#1 hits\, B sides and deep tracks - all performed
  with attention to detail duplicating their tight harmonies\, fancy guitar
  work and solid backbeat. In short\, that signature Beatles sound! \n\nBa
 sed in Connecticut\, these 5 lads\, started out a few years back perfectin
 g their music and vocal harmonies as they grew a list of songs now nearing
  100! Performing at special events\, outdoor concerts\, libraries\, restau
 rants and music festivals is the primary focus as their following grows wi
 th each performance. "No wigs\, costumes\, backing tracks or gimmicks here
 .... just 5 guys who sing and play like The Beatles!"\n\nEnjoy some delici
 ous cuisine from one of our Tuesdays in Plaza food vendors starting at 5:0
 0 p.m.:\n\nTacos Don Tacos\n\nHealdsburger\n\nChef Degen\n\nLola's Market\
 n\nPacheco Roasted Corn\n\nTuesdays in the Plaza is hosted by the City of 
 Healdsburg Community Services. A very special thank you to Big John's Mar
 ket for their generous sponsorship.
LOCATION:Healdsburg Plaza
URL:https://healdsburg.gov/335/Tuesdays-in-the-Plaza
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Line Dancing Workshop for Beginners
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260526T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260526T210000
UID:260511Lx1xExjUlkiQTJ0PFP-Y1w
DESCRIPTION:This Session\n\nEvent Series \\(See All\\)\n\nSaturday\, May 2
 3\, 2026 from 4:00 pm to 7:00 pm\n\nWorkshop from 4:00 PM – 5:00 PM Soci
 al from 5:00 PM – 7:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 110\n\nExperience Level\n\
 nBeginning\n\nEvent Category: Dance\n\nAge\\(s\\)\n\n18 and older\n\nRegis
 tration\n\nSocial Only:\n\n$15\n\nWorkshop & Social:\n\n$40\n\nReady to tr
 y line dancing—or get more confident on the floor? Join us for a fun\, w
 elcoming Beginner Line Dancing Workshop and Social\, designed especially f
 or absolute beginners and those who have never line danced before.\n\nAbou
 t the Class\n\nReady to try line dancing-or get more confident on the floo
 r? Join us for a fun\, welcoming Beginner Line Dancing Workshop and Social
 \, designed especially for absolute beginners and those who have never lin
 e danced before. The event includes three hours of structured Beginner–I
 mprover instruction\, where you’ll learn foundational steps\, easy-to-fo
 llow dances\, and build confidence at a comfortable pace. No experience re
 quired-just show up ready to move and have fun. Our instructors break ever
 ything down clearly\, making it approachable\, supportive\, and stress-fre
 e. After the workshop\, enjoy three hours of an open social dance\, where 
 you can practice what you’ve learned\, dance at your own pace\, and enjo
 y a relaxed\, friendly atmosphere. Dances will be beginner-friendly\, with
  plenty of opportunities to jump in or take a break as needed. Come solo o
 r bring friends-no partner needed. Whether you’re brand new\, curious ab
 out line dancing\, or looking for a fun night of movement and music\, this
  event is the perfect place to start.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/line-dancing-workshop-for-b
 eginners/2026-05-23/
