BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wine Tails Trail at Cuvaison Winery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260527T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260527T170000
UID:26050815-Sm14cNkiTCOaQw1qXpw
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy a new way to experience Cuvaison with your canine compan
 ion on the Wine Tails Trail. This self-guided vineyard walk winds just und
 er a mile through our Los Carneros estate\, with QR code stops highlightin
 g the history of our vines and winemaking. Guests begin their adventure by
  checking in with our Concierge for a map and orientation before setting o
 ff on the trail.\n\nAfter the walk\, return to the estate and enjoy a seat
 ed tasting of our current release wines\, while your pup relaxes by your s
 ide and enjoys a selection of “Barkuterie.” The Wine Tails Trail is a 
 chance to stretch your legs\, explore the vineyard\, and savor Cuvaison in
  the company of your best friend.\n\nWhen booking this experience\, please
  plan for the dog walk to begin at the time you select. The walk itself av
 erages about 45 minutes\, though you’ll also check in with our Concierge
  before and after\, as well as complete a quick waiver at the start. Your 
 wine tasting will be scheduled 60 minutes after your selected walk time\, 
 allowing a smooth transition from the trail back to your seated experience
 .\n\nGroup Size: Up to 4 guests\, including non-tasters\n\nDuration: Pleas
 e allow 120 minutes for this experience
LOCATION:Cuvaison Experience Salon\, Outdoors Only
URL:https://tewines.com/pages/cuvaison-tastings 
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:INTO THE LIGHT: Light-filled aintings by Katy Boggs
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260527T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260527T170000
UID:260501AVkdsnvgeUabYBmu1bejYg
DESCRIPTION:Katy's paintings are an exploration of light—how it shapes f
 orm\, reveals color\, and defines what we see.\n\n"I am drawn to moments w
 here light is felt as much as seen: filtering through dense leaves\, tower
 ing in the crowns of trees\, glinting off cresting waves\, or softening in
 to the quiet glow of a sunset. Light is everywhere\; without it\, there is
  no seeing. Beyond its physical presence\, it also carries a deeper resona
 nce as a symbol of hope. In a time of uncertainty\, this work seeks to bri
 ng light into the image\, both visually and metaphorically."\n\nReception:
  April 25\, 4 to 6 pm.
LOCATION:Sebastopol Gallery
URL:http://sebastopolgallery.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Abstract Vision
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260527T110500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260527T170000
UID:260424t9E8Sdux70Gp5fxUpEEBaA
DESCRIPTION:Abstract art moves beyond representation\, with a strong empha
 sis on shape\, color and form. Abstract art has the power to evoke emotion
 s\, appeal to our senses and transcend the physical world. Abstract expres
 sion captures the delicate\, elusive\, powerful and radiant energies that 
 fly under the radar of explanation.\n\nExhibition Artists: Dahlo (Marcela 
 Cabrera)\, Tess Abts\, Erika Adkins\, Bev Barnett\, Tara Belkin Harvey\, C
 ynthia Brodie\, Deborah Chaney\, Sharon Crary\, Alyson Dobbert\, Dianne Je
 an Erickson\, Kristine Goldenberg\, Beth Hall\, Sarah Harvey\, Ann Kalb-Ki
 p\, Debra Kreck­Harnish\, Michelle Nishikatsu\, Katy Parks Wilson\, D. Mi
 mi Read\, Elizabeth Springs\, Carol Tacconi\, Deborah Titus\, Chris Vetran
 o\, Mike Wasden\, Kim Winter\, Tara Yellen\, Kay Young\, Sabina Zildzic
LOCATION:Healdsburg Center for the Arts
URL:https://healdsburgcenterforthearts.org/an-abstract-vision/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
