BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Carry It With You
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T190000
UID:260508YceJTcZUzk2MxDAvwwgfRQ
DESCRIPTION:Exhibition Details\n\nCeramic Resident Artist Ariana Stein’s
  \\(She/They\\) debut solo exhibition.\n\nLOCATION Gallery 212\, Sonoma Co
 mmunity Center\n\nON VIEW May 30 – June 24\n\nOpening Reception Saturday
 \, May 30 · 5 – 7 PM Artist Talk 6 PM\n\nADMISSION Free & Open to the P
 ublic\n\nAbout This Exhibition\n\nCarry it with you is Ariana Stein’s \
 \(she/they\\) debut solo exhibition. Ari’s work is deeply rooted in folk
  tradition\, both through their Hungarian-American heritage\, and lineage 
 in North Carolina pottery apprenticeship. As a child of immigrants living 
 in America\, Ari values the importance of generational knowledge in a hype
 r-modern world. Carry it with you invites viewers to examine craft as an
  active conversation that marries past places\, cultures\, and people with
  the artist’s perspective here\, and now.\n\nArtist Statement\n\nAriana 
 Stein is a ceramic artist based in central North Carolina. She is a former
  apprentice to Kate Waltman and recipient of the 2025 Studio Potter Grant 
 for Apprenticeship Program. Ariana has exhibited her work across the USA a
 nd internationally. She has won numerous awards for her work\, including t
 he First Annual NCECA Creative Research Fellowship to pursue a body of wor
 k in her country of heritage\, Hungary\, in 2025. Ariana’s work combines
  historic making traditions from North Carolina pottery with the visual pa
 tterns and compelling folklore of Hungarian folk art.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/carry-it-with-you/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
