DESCRIPTION:AHA BLS Certification Class \\(Blended Learning\\)\n\nBLS Blen
 ded Learning / BLS Skills Session\n\nAHA BLS certification course for heal
 thcare providers. Blended Learning consists of an online course followed b
 y an in-person Skills Session. This American Heart Association Basic Life 
 Support class includes skills testing of cardiac and respiratory arrest ma
 nagement\, CPR\, AED use\, and choking treatment for all ages.\n\nAmerican
  Heart Association BLS Provider certifications are issued on the same day.
 \n\nLearn from a top-rated\, local CPR training company with over 900 5-st
 ar reviews! Our classes are fun\, engaging\, and expertly taught by experi
 enced first responders.\n\nLEARN MORE and ENROLL: https://vivecpr.com/clas
 s/heartcode-bls/\n\nCONTACT US: \\(707\\) 612-3277
LOCATION:Vive CPR
URL:https://vivecpr.com/class/heartcode-bls/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Once In A Blue (Full) Moon Hike
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T181500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T213000
UID:260428S_1N4p5DNUOOxWEJl2m5kw
DESCRIPTION:Bring a flashlight and your sense of wonder as you e
 xplore the park after dark during May's blue moon. This hike he
 ads up to the summit of Bald Mountain\, where we will see the
  moon rise over the Mayacamas and the sun set over Sonoma Vall
 ey. This is a strenuous hike of approximately 6.5 miles with 15
 00\\+ of vertical and some steep sections \\(not recommended for
  children under 12\\).\n\nMeet at the White Barn parking lot at
  least 10 minutes prior to the start time. Advance registration
  is $10 for general admission\, or $5 for youth \\(12-17 year 
 olds\\)\, students\, Sugarloaf members\, Sugarloaf or RFO volunteer
 s. All minors must be accompanied by a parent or legal guardian
 . You must register on this page to attend\; tickets on site a
 re $15 \\(exact change only\\) and might not be available. Bring 
 your flashlight\, at least a quart of water\, snacks\, and extra
  layers for the evening. Parking fees apply.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/2026bluemoon
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Paint Your Own Spirit Guide Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T120000
UID:260427kub-z-hkI0mfpRxClGBFbA
DESCRIPTION:Join the Spirit Guides artists\, Jacobo Ángeles and María 
 Ángeles\, for a vibrant\, hands-on workshop where you’ll paint your own
  wooden nahualito—a small spirit guide inspired by the rich traditions o
 f Zapotec culture. Guided step-by-step by the artists\, you’ll explore t
 he symbolism\, stories\, and cultural meaning behind these fantastical cre
 atures while learning traditional painting techniques that bring each figu
 re to life. Their son\, Ricardo Ángeles\, will join the workshop as trans
 lator\, ensuring a welcoming and engaging experience for all participants.
  All materials are provided\, including a hand-carved wooden figurine with
  a pre-painted base coat\, paints\, brushes\, an instructional booklet\, a
 nd a carrying bag—everything you need to create and take home your own u
 nique spirit guide. Whether you’re an experienced artist or simply curio
 us to learn\, this is a rare opportunity to connect directly with master a
 rtisans and immerse yourself in a joyful\, creative tradition. No previous
  painting experience is necessary\, and all skill levels are warmly welcom
 e. Participants of all ages are invited to join\; however\, children 12 an
 d under must be accompanied by a registered adult.
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
URL:https://sonomabg.org/visit/spirit-guides/#may
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
