BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Horses and Healers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T153000
UID:260422K88rw-uEjUKvxOZMMUJfyw
DESCRIPTION:Horses & Healers: Equine-Assisted Experiential Methods for Str
 engthening Clinical Presence\n\nNovato\, California — May 30th — Horse
 s & Healers: Equine-Assisted Experiential Methods for Strengthening Clinic
 al Presence will take place on May 30th from 9:30am to 3:30pm in Novato\, 
 California\, hosted by Heart & Mind Equine.\n\nThis in-person workshop is 
 designed for medical\, mental health\, and holistic professionals seeking 
 to strengthen clinical presence through experiential learning with horses.
 \n\nParticipants will engage in guided\, ground-based interactions with ho
 rses to explore clinical presence\, attunement\, communication\, and relat
 ional awareness. Horses provide real-time feedback to human emotional stat
 es and nonverbal communication\, offering an experiential approach to prof
 essional development.\n\nNo horse experience is required.\n\nEvent Details
 \n\nEvent: Horses & Healers: Equine-Assisted Experiential Methods for Stre
 ngthening Clinical Presence\n\nDate: May 30\n\nTime: 9:30 AM – 3:30 PM\n
 \nLocation: Novato\, California\n\nHost: Heart & Mind Equine\n\nFor more i
 nformation or to register\, visit: https://heart-mind-equine.mykajabi.com/
 horses-and-healers
LOCATION:Heart Mind Equine Horse Rescue
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/horses-and-healers/1862
 7209/2026-05-30T09
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Callie Watts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T000000
UID:260416E6w9nfk-iUm02Eqwn0TNRA
DESCRIPTION:Callie Watts is a singer/songwriter from Northern California w
 ho was raised on classical music\, The Beatles and The Beach Boys before d
 iscovering Joni Mitchell\, Elton John\, Stevie Wonder\, Paul Simon\, Billy
  Joel\, Carole King\, and all the great writers of the ’60s and 70’s w
 ho have influenced her sound and writing style. After graduating high scho
 ol\, Callie began playing and performing solo\, as well as in local and ba
 y area bands of different genres. She’s played blues with Eric Lindell a
 nd the Reds\, funky soul with Phatty\, and jazz/swing with Savoy Swingers 
 along with many other various projects. Callie has taken turns throughout 
 her career as a keyboardist\, guitarist\, writer\, and lead/backing vocali
 st\, and she’s currently a member of the dynamic Sonoma County funk rock
  band Burrows and Dilbeck\, having joined in 2010 as part of the former ba
 nd Frobeck. Over time\, she’s had the honor of opening for acts such as 
 Bootsy Collins\, Elvin Bishop\, Huey Lewis and The News\, War\, Ozomatli\,
  Bill Champlin\, Booker T\, and the B52s. Callie continues to perform freq
 uently as an acoustic solo artist\, focusing on developing a core audience
  and a buzz for her original material. Come hang out and listen at venues 
 such as Aroma Roasters\, Rincon Valley Tap Room and Bottle Shop\, and Hopm
 onk Tavern.
LOCATION:Belly Left Coast Kitchen & Taproom
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108193416?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Floral Fantasia
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T180000
UID:2604156TuxGP1QzEeGIT5ZAU2QbA
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  4/14/26\n\n**MAY EXHIBIT: FLORAL
  FANTASIA**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  April 27  –  May 31\, 2026\n\n**RECEPT
 ION: SATURDAY\, MAY 2\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet BEV HALEY and LUBA 
 STOLPER\;  Learn about their art and celebrate the show.  Be sure to tak
 e part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a beautiful work by a
  Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.**\n\nSonoma County artist\
 , **Bev Haley\,** unveils new floral works in acrylic that greet Spring wi
 th bountiful blooms and buds guaranteed to warm the viewer’s heart.  De
 signed with a whimsical flare\, each grouping of flowers in these works co
 alesce into harmonious synchronicity.  White and yellow flowers mix it up
  with joyful abandon in “Spring Fling Bouquet.”  A bird joins the par
 ty in “Sunny Side Up\,” a vibrant floral display – reds\, yellows\, 
 blues and more come together like a jeweled mosaic.  “I have always lov
 ed to paint flowers – they’re a simple subject with endless possibilit
 ies\, “noted Haley.  The viewer is rewarded with delicious examples of 
 Haley’s creative approach to those “endless possibilities” with this
  dynamic collection.\n\nPassionate about art\, Haley has tackled multiple 
 subjects but finds herself drawn to flowers.  Her first painting was a si
 ngle daisy in a blue vase.  Working from her reference – books and phot
 os – she composes on the canvas\, creatively applying colors and stylizi
 ng shapes towards a harmonious overall design.  Haley studied art at Sant
 a Rosa J.C. and with multiple master painters.  After retiring from a cha
 llenging business career\, she found her niche in acrylics and mixed media
 .  She has exhibited regionally and in Puerto Vallarta\, Mexico.\n\nMeet 
 the artist: Haley will be hosting the Gallery on May 9 & 23 from 11am to 6
  pm.\n\n The Stairway Smallworks Showcase features **Luba Stolper’s The
  Still Life Tradition\,** a collection of works in oil\, painted in the tr
 aditional style\, building luminosity through time-consuming layers of gla
 zing. One can almost taste the cherries in “Cherry Blossom” or smell t
 he pear in “Night Ritual.”  Masterfully rendered\, these paintings ar
 e so enticing\, one is tempted to reach through the frame to grab a cherry
  to see if it’s real.  Each work seems to capture the viewer in suspend
 ed reality.\n\nMeet the artist: Stolper will be hosting the Gallery on May
  2 & 11 from 11am to 6 pm and May 30 from 11am to 2:30pm.\n\nAlso join us 
 for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG**\, Thursday\, May 7\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART NITE He
 aldsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of Every Month\, is a community event cel
 ebrating art and creativity with over 20 galleries participating.  ArtNit
 eHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\, Healdsburg\
 , CA 95448. (707) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.    **www.upstai
 rsart gallery.net** \n\nFor further information: Contact: Beverly Bird\, P
 ress Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Park Rx-Beginner Hiking for Fitness Spring 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T080000
