BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Talking about Venus at Robert Ferguson Observatory
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260605T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260605T223000
UID:260516uF2qVTqNIkCvynX9NolCVA
DESCRIPTION:Discover the beauty and mystery of Venus during this special F
 ocus Night exploring one of the brightest and most fascinating planets in 
 our solar system. The evening begins with an engaging presentation coverin
 g Venus's thick cloud cover\, extreme surface temperatures\, runaway green
 house effect\, and its importance in astronomy and human history. Guests w
 ill also learn how ancient civilizations tracked Venus across the sky and 
 how modern space missions have revealed more about the planet's hidden sur
 face. After the presentation\, visitors can observe Venus through the obse
 rvatory's telescopes\, watching its changing phases as it moves through th
 e solar system. Perfect for both beginners and experienced stargazers\, th
 is immersive evening offers a deeper understanding of our brilliant neighb
 oring planet.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://www.sonoma.com/event/talking-about-venus-at-robert-ferguson-ob
 servatory/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
