SUMMARY:Sunday Swing Night at Hall of the Above
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260607T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260607T190000
UID:260504hjfV2gR5akCywpUNqygR9A
DESCRIPTION:Join us on the first Sunday of every month for SUNDAY SWING NI
 GHT at *Hall of the Above*\n\n🎷 Featuring a new-to-HOTA band\, The doRi
 aN Mode! 🎷\n\nThe doRiaN Mode explores the Great American Songbook as i
 t dishes up vintage jazz\, swinging R&B\, and soulful ballads\, from the s
 ounds of 1920s speakeasies and 1930s big-band swing to 1940s jump blues an
 d the rollicking R&B of Ruth Brown. Vocalist and bassist Dorian Bartley l
 eads this Petaluma-based acoustic quartet featuring Robby Elfman on piano/
 clarinet\, Peter Graves on sax\, and Tony Blake on drums. Whether they’
 re stomping at the Savoy in salute to Count Basie or paying homage to R&B 
 legend Etta James\, the doRiaN Mode brings elegance to classic American mu
 sic.\n\n💃🏻 Jasmine Worrell\, the Bay Area’s top swing dance instru
 ctor\, will offer a class from 4:15 – 5:00\n\n👯 Followed by live musi
 c and an open dance floor until 7:00 PM\n\n🎟️ $25 for admission inclu
 des the class — cash at the door. Kids 12 and under are free.\n\n🕺
 🏾 All skill levels welcome\; no partner required.\n\nSee you on the dan
 ce floor!
LOCATION:Hall of the Above
URL:https://www.halloftheabove.com/event-database/swing-dancing-at-hall-of
 -the-above-87jr4-tf756-m2l57-33xey-n2f47
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
