BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Death Curious Workshop:  Prepare with Care - Live with Joy!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260608T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260608T163000
UID:260515FGm8Flf6QUC1gZdyMpeqgw
DESCRIPTION:Most of us mean to do it. Few of us do.\n\nThe people who will
  care for you — or care for your affairs — need more than good intenti
 ons. They need documents\, passwords\, account numbers\, and to know where
  things are. In a world where so much of life lives online\, an undocument
 ed digital life can stop everything cold.\n\nWhether you have a close circ
 le or are navigating life more independently\, getting organized is one of
  the most concrete acts of care you can offer. The earlier\, the kinder.\n
 \nJoin End of Life Doula Linda Suhr for a practical\, step-by-step worksho
 p covering the ten essential areas of end-of-life preparation — so the p
 eople you trust\, or the systems that will serve you\, can do their job.
LOCATION:Healdsburg Senior Center
URL:http://whenthetimecomes.org
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wine Tails Trail at Cuvaison Winery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260608T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260608T170000
UID:260508z_J7XSPxxk2qMaLqUfozDQ
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy a new way to experience Cuvaison with your canine compan
 ion on the Wine Tails Trail. This self-guided vineyard walk winds just und
 er a mile through our Los Carneros estate\, with QR code stops highlightin
 g the history of our vines and winemaking. Guests begin their adventure by
  checking in with our Concierge for a map and orientation before setting o
 ff on the trail.\n\nAfter the walk\, return to the estate and enjoy a seat
 ed tasting of our current release wines\, while your pup relaxes by your s
 ide and enjoys a selection of “Barkuterie.” The Wine Tails Trail is a 
 chance to stretch your legs\, explore the vineyard\, and savor Cuvaison in
  the company of your best friend.\n\nWhen booking this experience\, please
  plan for the dog walk to begin at the time you select. The walk itself av
 erages about 45 minutes\, though you’ll also check in with our Concierge
  before and after\, as well as complete a quick waiver at the start. Your 
 wine tasting will be scheduled 60 minutes after your selected walk time\, 
 allowing a smooth transition from the trail back to your seated experience
 .\n\nGroup Size: Up to 4 guests\, including non-tasters\n\nDuration: Pleas
 e allow 120 minutes for this experience
LOCATION:Cuvaison Experience Salon\, Outdoors Only
URL:https://tewines.com/pages/cuvaison-tastings 
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:MAD Science Camp at Hanna Center
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260608T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260608T160000
UID:260504APW_vc5geE-5-bwpqfdCFQ
DESCRIPTION:Get ready for a week of fun experiments\, hands-on activities\
 , and exciting scientific discoveries with Instructor Phil Amormino! This
  camp will introduce campers to the fascinating world of science\, from ch
 emistry experiments to physics challenges. Campers will learn scientific p
 rinciples in a fun\, interactive way and develop critical thinking skills 
 while engaging in hands-on experiments that bring science to life.
LOCATION:Hanna Center
URL:https://hannacenter.org/services/community/camps/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Secret Agent Camp - Sonoma Gymnastics Academy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260608T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260608T143000
UID:260314k5xU0CLWV0unqAO6PdJmWQ
DESCRIPTION:Make the most of summer with award-winning Gymnastics Camps at
  SGA! Keep children’s bodies and brains active with careful guidance fro
 m our trained instructors\, and have some fun\, too. We’ll play in our o
 utdoor inflatable water parks\, eat lunch in the park\, and learn basic gy
 mnastics techniques every day from 8:30 AM - 2:30 PM. Each week has its ow
 n unique theme with specialized crafts\, games\, activities\, and learning
 . Enroll in one week\, a few\, or all ten! Sign up on our site\, email us\
 , or call us to register. Spots are limited.\n\n\\-This week’s theme is:
  SECRET AGENT WEEK!-\n\nTuck and roll into this week's Secret Agent Camp! 
 Campers will solve mysteries together with block towers to set the scene. 
 Leap from one mat to another\, hide behind blocks\, tuck and roll over equ
 ipment and become the best Secret Agent ever! Campers will craft their own
  secret agent badges with their photos\, and get to play with new friends 
 or “agent partners”. Campers will spend their days with Parkour style 
 games\, obstacle courses\, mystery games\, Secret Agent crafts\, and learn
 ing Gymnastics skills!\n\nCamps are best suited for children ages 4 to 12.
  All participants must be fully toilet-trained.\n\nStudents should wear a 
 t-shirt with elastic waistband shorts/pants\, or a leotard. Long hair must
  be pulled back. No jewelry\, jeans\, dresses\, or skirts. Please wear or 
 pack clothing layers for if the weather permits us to adventure outside!\n
 \nPlease pack your child(ren) a PEANUT-FREE lunch\, water bottle\, and com
 fortable shoes. Morning snacks will be provided.
LOCATION:Sonoma Gymnastics Academy
URL:https://sonomagymnasticsacademy.com/camps/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Brainstormer Trivia with Rick Tosh
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260608T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260608T210000
