BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wildfire and Smoke Ready Talk - Free for all Sonoma County Adults
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260609T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260609T140000
UID:260519oZCoc9Y5kkiLL91T_kgpig
DESCRIPTION:Fire Inspector Charles Hall with the Sonoma County Fire Distri
 ct will explain the outlook for our current wildfire year and explain how 
 you can protect your home and property by taking easy steps now to decreas
 e your risks. The threat of wildfire smoke and how to protect yourself and
  family will also be discussed. Did you know N95 masks do not protect from
  all toxins in wildfire smoke?\n\nA combination lantern/flashlight will be
  included\, while supplies last\, one per family. The talk is free for all
  County adults to attend\, so please share this invite. To register go to 
 **https://bit.ly/WindsorWildfirePrep** or call the Senior Center at 707-83
 8-1260. Pre-registration is not required but is recommended for the giveaw
 ay. This presentation is part of the Windsor Ready Talk series hosted by t
 he Town of Windsor and Windsor COPE. For more information email windsor\\_
 cope@yahoo.com
