UID:260514SHZ2Dfyr9kWEG-8u_QabBw
DESCRIPTION:This year\, we're bringing something different! Introducing ou
 r first-ever Pride Concert and Drag Show at Sebastiani Theatre featuring a
 ll queer talent\, fierce performances\, and pure Pride! Drag Performances 
 You’re in for a night of drag from two Bay Area legends—Kochina Rude\,
  your host and Sonoma County native\, and Tila Pia\, an infamous stunt que
 en who’s turned looks from Hawaii to New York. Headliner Band Headlining
  the night is J. Graves\, a queer\, non-binary band out of Portland\, know
 n for their dynamic live sound—blending guitar-driven energy with bold v
 ocals and a mix of original songs and covers like Sex and Candy and Dancin
 g on My Own. Expect a show that moves—between music\, drag\, and moments
  that pull the whole room in. This isn’t something Sonoma sees every day
 . This first annual concert is also a fundraiser for Sonoma Valley Pride\,
  supporting future events\, visibility\, and community programming right h
 ere in Sonoma. Every ticket helps build what comes next. Come ready to dan
 ce\, show up\, and be part of it. Sponsored and made possible by by WakeUp
  Sonoma\, Out In The Vineyard\, Matthew Long Design\, No Sleep No Hunger
LOCATION:Sebastiani Theatre
